>> title: Skillet Lasagna
>> category: Pasta
>> tags: pasta, sausage, tomatoes, one-pot, skillet, weeknight
>> counters: One Pot
>> aka: one-pan lasagna, lazy lasagna, broken lasagna, skillet lasagne
>> servings: 4
>> time: 50 min
>> washing-up: the cast-iron skillet
>> keeps: 2 days — it firms into proper slices overnight, which some people prefer; cover it or the edges dry

>> step: The noodles go in dry and broken and cook in the sauce, and the starch they shed is what thickens it.
The noodles go in dry and broken, and they cook in the sauce rather than in a pot of water beside it.

>> step: brown 8 min, broken up
Brown @Italian sausage{1%lb}(450 g; casings off) in @olive oil{1%Tbs} in a #cast-iron skillet{} for ~brown{8%min}.

>> step: soften 4 min
Soften @&(~1)sausage{} with @yellow onion{1%medium}(diced), @garlic{4%cloves}(sliced), @dried oregano{1%tsp}, @red pepper flakes{1/2%tsp} for ~saute{4%min}.

>> step: simmer covered 20 min, noodles under the sauce
Simmer @&(~1)base{} covered with @canned crushed tomatoes{28%oz}(800 g), @water{1 1/2%cups}(360 mL), @lasagna noodles{8%oz}(225 g; broken in 2-in pieces), @kosher salt{1 1/2%tsp} for ~simmer{20%min}.

>> step: spoon the cheese on, stand covered 5 min
Dot @&(~1)skillet lasagna{} with @whole-milk ricotta{1%cup}(250 g), @low-moisture mozzarella{1%cup}(115 g; shredded), @basil{1/4%cup}(torn) and ~stand{5%min} covered off the heat.

>> step: Push the noodles under the liquid before the lid goes on and stir once at ten minutes, or the tops go leathery.
Push the noodles under the liquid before the lid goes on and stir once at the ten-minute mark, or the pieces on top come out leathery at the edges.
